{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (46.67%) to predicted peptide 5 F=K: 15%, R: 23%. Activity: Active against Gram+ bacteria S. aureus CGMCC 1.2465 and 5 MRSA strains QZ19131-19134 (MIC 6-12 uM), S. epidermidis CGMCC 1.4260 (MIC 3-6 uM), B. subtilis CGMCC 1.3358 (MIC 12-24 uM), L. monocytogenes CGMCC 1.4260 (MIC 24-48 uM), Gram- P. fluorescens CGMCC 1.3202 (MIC 6-12 uM), A. baumannii CGMCC 1.6769 (MIC 12-24 uM), P. aeruginosa CGMCC 1.2421 and 5 MDR strains QZ18071-18077 (MIC 6-12 uM), P. stutzeri CGMCC 1.1803 (MIC 1.5-3 uM), E. coli CGMCC 1.2389 (MIC 12-24 uM). MBC values are slightly higher. Killed S. aureus in the cultural supernatant of RAW 264.7 cells. Antibiofilm B: inhibited biofilm formation. Antimicrobial robustness: NaCl-insensitive:S. aureus 1.2465 (160 mM); NaCl-insensitive:P. aeruginosa 1.2421 (160 mM). MOA:bacteria:S. aureus: MOA:bacteria:P. aeruginosa: permeated bacterial membranes. Induced ROS release. Resistance development:no:bacteria:S. aureus MRSA QZ19134: Resistance development:no:bacteria:P. aeruginosa QZ1807: no resistance observed after 50 passages. cf. MRSA MIC increased >4096 fold for ntibiotic rifampicin. In vitro toxicity: not toxic to murine hepatic cell line AML 12, uman hepatic cell line L02, hepatocellular carcinoma cell line HepG2, and NSCLC cell line NCI-H46 at 96 uM (TC50 >> 100 uM). Recombinant production:yeast:Pichia pastoris: multiple copy expression increased yield by 2.75 fold. Peptide yield: 126.1 mg/L ( Dong et al., 2025).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36061863", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Cell Infect Microbiol. 2022 Aug 2;12:928220. doi: 10.3389/fcimb.2022.928220. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP06294", "source_id": "AP06294", "source_numeric_id": "06294", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP06294", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "A truncated peptide Spgillcin177-189 derived from mud crab Scylla paramamosain exerting multiple antibacterial activities", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
